Implement the layer mask blend in Vulkan and WebGPU depthStencil mode.

- source/renderer/vulkan/draw_pipeline_vulkan.cpp: Vulkan layer mask: build the BlendEquation::layerMask fixed-function blend (src ZERO, dst SRC_ALPHA, op ADD) so depthStencil mode can apply a layer mask like the GL backend. vk_blend_op case.
- source/renderer/vulkan/draw_pipeline_vulkan.cpp: Vulkan layer mask: add vk_src_blend_factor(), returning ZERO for layerMask and ONE otherwise.
- source/renderer/vulkan/draw_pipeline_vulkan.cpp: Vulkan layer mask: vk_dst_blend_factor case returns SRC_ALPHA for layerMask.
- source/renderer/vulkan/draw_pipeline_vulkan.cpp: Vulkan layer mask: feed vk_src_blend_factor() into the color/alpha src blend factors instead of a hardcoded ONE.
- source/renderer/vulkan/render_context_vulkan_impl.cpp: Vulkan layer mask: advertise supportsDepthStencilLayerMask now that the pipeline builder implements the blend, so masks apply on devices without raster ordering (e.g. most mobile GPUs).
- source/renderer/webgpu/render_context_webgpu_impl.cpp: WebGPU layer mask: advertise supportsDepthStencilLayerMask now that makeDrawPipeline builds the blend; YUP forces masked layers into depthStencil mode (atomic mode has no layer-mask op).
- source/renderer/webgpu/render_context_webgpu_impl.cpp: WebGPU layer mask: wgpuBlendOp case returns ADD for layerMask (src ZERO, dst SRC_ALPHA).
- source/renderer/webgpu/render_context_webgpu_impl.cpp: WebGPU layer mask: wgpuDstBlendFactor case returns SRC_ALPHA for layerMask, and add wgpuSrcBlendFactor() returning ZERO for layerMask.
- source/renderer/webgpu/render_context_webgpu_impl.cpp: WebGPU layer mask: feed wgpuSrcBlendFactor() into the blend component src factor instead of a hardcoded ONE.

